        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat: allow custom sandbox image tags",
        "body": "AI-assisted: yes — implementation and review used Codex; the author verified the resulting code and behavior.\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nSandbox setup always builds the fixed `openclaw-sandbox:bookworm-slim` tag, preventing deployments from producing revision-scoped images for safe rollout and rollback.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nAllow `OPENCLAW_SANDBOX_IMAGE` to select the build tag while preserving the existing tag when the variable is unset. Runtime image selection is unchanged.\n\n## User Impact\n\nOperators can build immutable, independently tagged sandbox images. Existing setup commands retain their current behavior.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `node_modules/.bin/vitest run test/scripts/docker-build-helper.test.ts`\n- `git diff --check -- scripts/sandbox-setup.sh test/scripts/docker-build-helper.test.ts`\n",
